.claude/

# Post-session transcript fixtures mirror real CLI home directories, so their
# paths are made of dot-directories: `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.gigacode/`,
# `.deepseek/`. The `.claude/` rule above is unanchored, so it also matched
# `tests/fixtures/postsession/home/.claude/`, and git never lists ignored
# files -- `git status` stayed silent while the Claude adapter's only fixtures
# were missing from the commit and the suite went green against the working
# tree alone. Re-include the whole fixture root rather than one dot-directory,
# so a later rule naming any of the others cannot re-open the same hole. The
# directory has to be re-included *before* its contents: a file under an
# excluded directory cannot be negated, because git never descends into it.
!tests/fixtures/postsession/
!tests/fixtures/postsession/**

# Post-session corpus index: one compact row per accumulated transcript. It is
# thousands of absolute paths under the user's home directory and is rebuilt
# from disk by `scripts/postsession_corpus.py --build`, so tracking it would
# add ~4000 churning lines for no evidence. The seal beside it --
# artifacts/post-session/corpus.json, which is tracked -- carries
# `index_sha256` over exactly these bytes, so a rebuilt index still has to
# prove it is the one the manifest sealed.
artifacts/post-session/corpus-index.jsonl

# Schema-trigger replay outputs of the sfx field store (event and node ids of
# private memory). `scripts/schema_trigger_replay.py run` regenerates them
# locally from a snapshot; the numbers are reported in
# artifacts/schema-trigger/report-3.md. They are never committed, so they
# reach neither alt nor the external repository.
artifacts/schema-trigger/v2/original-sfx.json
artifacts/schema-trigger/v2/new-sfx.json
artifacts/schema-trigger/v3/
